    "summary": "High‑energy set with smoking Casey Jones and piano‑driven Ramble On Rose",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a crisp soundboard capture of a high‑energy night, highlighted by a blistering Casey Jones and a powerful Black Peter. Keith’s piano adds sparkle to the debut of Ramble On Rose, while Phil’s bass drives the groove throughout. Overall performance is tight with standout moments from Tennessee Jed and One More Saturday Night.",
    "review": "December 9, 1971 at St. Louis’ Fox Theatre finds the Dead in top form, rolling out a set that crackles with excitement from start to finish. The first set builds momentum through classic rockers like Truckin' and Jack Straw before launching into a smoking Casey Jones that segues straight into an exuberant One More Saturday Night. Phil’s bass is front‑and‑center, powering the band’s drive, while Jerry recovers quickly after a minor flub on Brown Eyed Women. The second set shines with Keith Godchaux’s piano‑driven Ramble On Rose—its slightly distorted charm adds a playful edge—and a rousing Black Peter that showcases the group’s tight interplay. Closing with a two‑part Not Fade Away medley, the night captures the band’s early‑70s vitality and sets a high bar for the era.",
